# eu-u9xj.6 (PP) — metadata crosses the parallel boundary with its value, so
# metadata that is not itself data is a boundary error, exactly as a
# non-serialisable result is (spec §6).
#
# The alternative would be to drop it, and dropping it is the one option that
# is not available: `par-map` promises to be identical to `map`, and `map`
# keeps the annotation. A `:suppress` silently lost across the boundary would
# re-expose a key its author marked internal, with no error and no visible
# difference in the value — `=` ignores metadata.
#
# This is a divergence from `map`, which carries an unevaluated function in
# metadata without complaint. It is the documented consequence of `par-*`
# being strict and process-crossing, and it is loud rather than silent.
mk(x): { ` { checker: (_0 + 1) } odd: x
          v: x }
result: [1, 2] par-map(mk)
